  "recovery_criteria": "Recovered: one linked track (3 or more visits) has detections within 2 px (about 12 arcsec) of the injected position in at least 3 separate visits. False positive: a linked track that matches no injection and no real mover found in the unmodified images.",
  "method_notes": [
    "Synthetic sources are added to the real SPHEREx Level 2 cutouts of each field after zodiacal-light and background subtraction, using each exposure's own PSF (PSF extension, nearest of 121 zones, 10x oversampled, integrated over native pixels).",
    "Flux is flat in F_nu (the same AB magnitude at every wavelength SPHEREx samples).",
    "Photon noise from the source is added with the variance-versus-signal slope measured from each exposure's own IMAGE and VARIANCE extensions.",
    "Linear tracks move at a fixed rate in a random direction. Distance tracks are bodies at a fixed heliocentric distance on circular prograde orbits in the ecliptic, seen from SPHEREx's real position (Earth from astropy's built-in ephemeris plus the spacecraft position in each FITS header).",
    "12 sources per run, at least 150 arcsec apart at mid-visit, placed uniformly over the central 80% of the field; they can cross stars and leave the image.",
    "Detection and linking are the unmodified pipeline (detection threshold 4.5 sigma, at least 3 visits per track, linking rates 0.5-250 arcsec/hr).",
    "Intervals are Wilson 95% for fractions and Poisson 95% for the false-positive count."
  ],
